      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so if the signs are actually different for certain groups, does that mean the \"standard\" medical training we get is basically just training us to recognize symptoms in white people? like, is it more accurate to say that medicine is essentially built around a white baseline, and other races are just \"exceptions\" to the rule?",
